1 · The axis fix

Your TRUE NORTH table has three cross-wired entries. In standard 6-DOF marine dynamics, each physical axis carries exactly one translation and one rotation:

· X (longitudinal): Surge ↔ Roll
· Y (lateral): Sway ↔ Pitch
· Z (vertical): Heave ↔ Yaw

Your table assigned Heave → eX, Pitch → Zi, and Sway → eZ — each on the wrong physical axis. Corrected:

Symbol DOF Physical axis Motion Type
X Roll X tilting side ↔ side rotation
Xi Surge X forward ↔ backward translation
Y Pitch Y bow up ↔ bow down rotation
Yi Sway Y port ↔ starboard translation
Z Yaw Z turning left ↔ right rotation
Zi Heave Z up ↔ down translation

The rule: bare Cap = rotation on that axis, -i suffix = translation on the same axis. If you want to keep e-prefixed forms, e can only mean "elevation class" (Z-only), so eZ = Heave and eX/eY would be retired or aliased.

Your earlier architecture mapping stays valid after the fix:

X = Surge → progression / force
Y = Sway → lateral allocation / branching
Z = Heave → elevation / hierarchy

with rotations Roll = stability, Pitch = orientation, Yaw = navigation.

