4 · Register-safe notation, going forward

To prevent the same cross-wiring on any future token:

Marker Meaning Enforced register
bare Cap (X Y Z) rotation DOF D
-i suffix (Xi Yi Zi) translation DOF on same axis D
-e prefix (Z only) elevation class alias D
← → ↑↑ ↓↓ symbolic polarity M
§ transition probe M
∅ empty / null state M (also valid in O as set-theoretic)

Rule: if a token carries i or e, it is a translation and appears only in D. If it carries §, ←, →, ↑↑, or ↓↓, it is symbolic and appears only in M. No symbol crosses registers without an explicit re-label in the character register.

